cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these instruments, please cite them as below."
title: "ccd-instruments: Calibrator, evaluator, and value elicitor for the Countervailing Co-Deployment framework"
abstract: "Three offline, single-file browser instruments that fix the co-deployment level an automated decision system triggers, measure whether an existing claimant-side counterpart discharges that duty, and structure the value trade-off judgment the calibration depends on."
authors:
  - family-names: Panitz
    given-names: Vanessa
    affiliation: "University of Wisconsin Law School"
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/panitzvanessa/ccd-instruments"
keywords:
  - due process
  - administrative law
  - automated decision systems
  - public benefits
  - algorithmic accountability

